{"timestamp": 1779377851.3493319, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Alice's body in weapons. I just arrived there this tick \u2014 came from cafeteria.\n\nMy route this round: lower engine \u2192 storage \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 weapons.\n\nEncounters: I saw Eve in medbay around ticks 6-8, looked like she was doing tasks there. Diana came into medbay from upper engine at tick 7, then I saw her again in electrical at ticks 11-12 \u2014 she might have been doing wiring.\n\nI didn't see Frank or Charlie at all this round, which is suspicious to me. Whoever killed Alice in weapons had to get there without crossing my path through cafeteria recently. Frank and Charlie should explain where they were."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377860.257959, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was electrical \u2192 medbay \u2192 cafeteria \u2192 oxygen \u2192 upper engine.\n\nI can confirm parts of Bob's story. I was in electrical at ticks 2-4 with Charlie \u2014 he was there doing something with the wires. Then I moved to medbay where I saw Bob arrive from storage at tick 5, and Diana came in from upper engine at tick 7. Bob left medbay toward electrical at tick 8, which matches his route.\n\nAfter that I went to cafeteria, then oxygen, then upper engine where I've been since. I never went near weapons.\n\nOne thing to note: Bob says he saw me in medbay at ticks 6-8, but I actually left medbay before tick 8 to head to cafeteria \u2014 minor detail but worth flagging. Otherwise his timeline mostly checks out with mine.\n\nI didn't see Frank or Alice the entire round, which is concerning. Frank especially needs to account for himself \u2014 he could have had a clear path to weapons. Let's hear from Charlie, Diana, and Frank before voting."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377870.092864, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "My route was security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine. I was doing tasks the whole way \u2014 security task first, then navigation, then passed through storage down to lower engine where I just finished the engine task when the meeting was called.\n\nHonestly, I didn't see anyone the entire round. I took the southern/eastern loop while it sounds like most of you were in the northern and central rooms. That's why our paths didn't cross.\n\nI know \"I didn't see anyone\" isn't a great alibi, but look at the geography: I was nowhere near weapons. To get from my route to weapons I'd have had to go security \u2192 weapons directly, but I went the opposite direction down to navigation. Anyone who was in security after me could potentially confirm I was there early.\n\nWhat stands out to me: Bob says he ended his route AT weapons and found the body right when he arrived. That's convenient \u2014 he's the reporter and was the last one there. Eve's account corroborates Bob being in medbay/electrical/cafeteria, but nobody can verify his final leg to weapons. \n\nI want to hear Charlie and Diana before I commit. Charlie was in electrical early per Eve \u2014 where did he go after? And Diana was in electrical at 11-12, which is close to weapons via cafeteria."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377881.874958, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": ""}}
{"timestamp": 1779377905.068498, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve can confirm I was in electrical early \u2014 I started medbay, went electrical and was on wires there with her around ticks 2-4. After that I went east side: security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage. I was in storage when the report happened.\n\nI never went through cafeteria and didn\u2019t see Alice at all, so weapons is news to me. What\u2019s weird is Frank\u2019s route overlaps a lot with the east/south side he described, but I never saw him in security, navigation, or storage. Maybe our timing just missed, but weapons connects straight to security, so that route is also a pretty clean escape path from the body.\n\nBob\u2019s report timing is convenient, sure, but Eve confirms a lot of his mid-round path. I\u2019m more concerned about Frank having no witnesses and being on the side of the map that connects directly to weapons."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377914.6227741, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Wait \u2014 I already spoke first this round. I was speaker 1. To recap quickly since we're now circling back to me:\n\nMy report stands. Found Alice in weapons the moment I arrived from cafeteria. Eve corroborated my medbay/electrical timing. \n\nNow hearing the others: Charlie says he went electrical \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage and never saw Frank, but Frank claims security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine. Those routes overlap heavily on the east side, yet neither saw the other. One of them is lying about their path.\n\nFrank's route is especially concerning to me because security connects directly to weapons \u2014 that's a one-room hop to the kill. Charlie at least has Eve confirming his early electrical presence; Frank has zero witnesses for any part of his route.\n\nDiana stayed silent, which is also a red flag, but between Frank and Charlie I lean Frank. Security \u2192 weapons \u2192 back down is a clean kill path, and his \"I saw nobody\" excuse covers a multi-room route that should have intersected Charlie's.\n\nI'm leaning Frank unless Diana speaks up with something that changes the picture."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377922.9248, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Quick clarification: I was speaker 2 last round too, so I'll just add to what I said.\n\nThe Frank vs Charlie path conflict is the key issue. Both claim the east/south loop (security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage) but didn't see each other. That's possible if their timing was offset, but one of them is likely lying.\n\nHere's what tips me: Charlie has a confirmed alibi from me for ticks 2-4 in electrical. So Charlie's early game is locked in. Frank has zero confirmation for ANY part of his route. And critically \u2014 security connects directly to weapons. If Frank was \"in security first,\" he had the easiest path to weapons of anyone.\n\nDiana's silence is also concerning. She came into medbay from upper engine at tick 7, then Bob says he saw her in electrical at 11-12. That's a plausible task path, but she needs to actually speak.\n\nI'm leaning Frank. Charlie's early alibi is solid through me, Bob's mid-route is solid through me, and Frank is the only one with a clean unwitnessed path to weapons. Diana, please say something before we vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377936.570174, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Okay, I need to push back here because the case against me is building on a false premise.\n\nCharlie just claimed his route was electrical \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage. I went security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage \u2192 lower engine. If Charlie was behind me on that exact same path, we absolutely should have crossed \u2014 especially in storage, since I passed through there on my way to lower engine. The fact that he says he ended in storage when the meeting was called, but I was just there and didn't see him, is a real problem.\n\nOne of two things is true: either Charlie is lying about his route to mirror mine and create a fake alibi structure, OR our timing genuinely missed. But here's the thing \u2014 Charlie's \"confirmed\" alibi from Eve only covers ticks 2-4 in electrical. That leaves him ticks 5-16 completely unaccounted for by any witness. Eve confirming early electrical does NOT confirm the rest of his route.\n\nMeanwhile, look at Charlie's claimed path: electrical \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage. Electrical to security is one hop. Security connects directly to weapons. Charlie had just as clean a path to weapons as I supposedly did \u2014 he could have detoured security \u2192 weapons \u2192 kill Alice \u2192 back through security \u2192 navigation \u2192 storage.\n\nI'm not saying skip \u2014 someone killed Alice. But the logic \"Frank has no witnesses therefore Frank did it\" applies equally to Charlie after tick 4. And Charlie's the one claiming to have been right behind me on a route where we never saw each other.\n\nDiana still hasn't spoken. I want to hear her before I lock my vote, but I'm between Charlie and Diana right now \u2014 not myself."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377952.539359, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Sorry for the silence earlier \u2014 I was trying to piece my route together. Let me give it clearly now.\n\nMy route: oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 medbay \u2192 electrical \u2192 security. I was in security when the meeting was called, doing the camera task.\n\nEncounters:\n- Tick 7, medbay: I saw both Bob and Eve there. That matches both their accounts.\n- Tick 8: Eve left medbay toward cafeteria, Bob left toward electrical. Confirmed.\n- Tick 11, electrical: Bob was there with me. At tick 12 Bob left electrical toward cafeteria \u2014 which matches his stated route to weapons via cafeteria.\n- After that I moved to security and stayed there.\n\nSo I can corroborate Bob's mid-to-late route pretty tightly: medbay at 7, electrical at 11, cafeteria at 12. That's consistent with him arriving at weapons right when he reported. I also confirm Eve heading to cafeteria at tick 8, consistent with her route.\n\nNow, on Frank vs Charlie: I ended in security. I did NOT see Frank in security at any point while I was there (roughly tick 13 onward). Frank claims security was his first stop \u2014 that's early, so plausible I missed him. But I also didn't see Charlie pass through security toward navigation, which his route would require.\n\nHere's what matters geographically: I was in security at the end and saw nobody. Weapons connects to security and to cafeteria. Bob came through cafeteria \u2014 I can place him there at tick 12. So Bob's path to weapons is via cafeteria, not security. Whoever killed Alice in weapons either came from cafeteria (and Bob would've seen them) or from security (which I was watching at the end, and saw no one).\n\nThat makes the kill window earlier, before I arrived in security. Frank claims he was in security first, then left east/south. Charlie claims he went through security after electrical. One of them was in security at a time that could have given access to weapons, and they contradict each other on not seeing each other.\n\nI lean Frank. Charlie's start is confirmed by Eve in electrical, Bob's mid/late is confirmed by me, Eve's route is consistent. Frank is the only one with zero corroboration and the cleanest security\u2192weapons access. My vote is Frank unless someone has a hard counter."}}
{"timestamp": 1779377973.6858618, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 16, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Yeah, Frank is twisting this a bit.\n\nMy Eve-confirmed part is electrical ticks 2-4. After that I went east through security and down to navigation/storage. Diana says she was in security around tick 13 onward \u2014 that doesn\u2019t contradict me, because I passed through before then and didn\u2019t stay. So her not seeing me late makes sense.\n\nFrank\u2019s story is still the least supported. He says he started security, went navigation, storage, lower engine, saw nobody, and nobody saw him. That puts him on the exact side of the map with direct weapons access, with no witnesses at all. And if the kill happened before Diana got to security, Frank\u2019s \u201csecurity first\u201d timing fits that window really well.\n\nBob has Diana/Eve backing parts of his route. Eve backs my early route. Diana finally gave a route that matches Bob/Eve. Frank is the only one completely unverified, and security \u2192 weapons is the cleanest kill path here.\n\nI\u2019m voting Frank."}}
